# Local secrets — GEMINI_API_KEY and any other real credentials belong in
# the Netlify dashboard (Site configuration → Environment variables), never
# in a committed file. `.env` was already tracked before this was added
# (contains only Supabase's public anon key/URL, not a high-severity
# secret) — left as-is rather than untracked unilaterally, but no new
# secret-bearing env file should ever be committed going forward.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
netlify/functions/.env

